  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Education obligated $2.2B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Education made 639 awards with an average award size of $3.4M, and obligations fell 14.0% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a recent range between $2.2B and $2.7B, with FY21 at $2.7B, FY22 at $2.4B, FY23 at $2.4B, FY24 at $2.7B, FY25 at $2.5B, and FY26 at $2.2B. Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation and Computer Systems Design Services are the largest NAICS categories in FY2026 to date, at $947M and $657M respectively, followed by Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $144M. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC and NELNET SERVICING LLC are the top vendors in FY2026 to date at $338M and $291M respectively, with MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $251M and EDFINANCIAL SERVICES LLC at $198M rounding out the next tier. This snapshot covers contract obligations and reflects partial current-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What drove contract obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Education obligated $2.2B, with Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation accounting for $947M and Computer Systems Design Services accounting for $657M. The Department of Education made 639 awards, and the average award size was $3.4M. Obligations fell 14.0% year over year, reflecting lower totals compared with some prior years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and contract types dominate Education's spending?",
        "body": "ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC led vendors at $338M, followed by NELNET SERVICING LLC at $291M and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC at $251M. The Department of Education also obligated funds to EDFINANCIAL SERVICES LLC at $198M and MISSOURI HIGHER EDUCATION LOAN AUTHORITY at $161M. Top contract categories include credit intermediation activities, systems design, and social sciences R&D."
      }
    ]
